      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-312697",
      ":question/problem": "In triangle $ABC$, the measure of angle $A$ is $30^{\u2218}$ and the measure of angle $B$ is $100^{\u2218}$. In triangle $DEF$, the measure of angle $D$ is $30^{\u2218}$ and the measure of angle $E$ is $100^{\u2218}$. Which of the following additional pieces of information is needed to prove that the two triangles are similar?\n\n1. The measure of angle $C$ is $50^{\u2218}$.\n2. $AC = 1$ and $DF = 3$.\n3. The measure of angle $C$ is $50^{\u2218}$ and $DF = 3$.\n4. No additional information is needed."
